From: Samuel Rounce <me@samuelrounce.co.uk>
Subject: [PATCH] winewayland: Advertise VK_WINE_openvr/openxr_device_extensions

wineopenxr and vrclient hand DXVK and vkd3d-proton the pseudo-extensions
VK_WINE_openxr_device_extensions / VK_WINE_openvr_device_extensions, which
win32u expands into the runtime's real device extensions at vkCreateDevice.
Since "winevulkan: Check enabled device extensions support on the PE side"
(4812732aa46) the PE loader rejects any requested extension the display
driver did not advertise, so a device create that includes the pseudo
extension fails with VK_ERROR_EXTENSION_NOT_PRESENT. winex11 and nulldrv
set these flags in map_device_extensions; winewayland does not, so every
OpenXR title running under PROTON_ENABLE_WAYLAND=1 fails to create its
D3D11/D3D12 device (LMU: cubeDirectX Init_Device check failure).

diff --git a/dlls/winewayland.drv/vulkan.c b/dlls/winewayland.drv/vulkan.c
index 543d2b4284d..6a08d62421a 100644
--- a/dlls/winewayland.drv/vulkan.c
+++ b/dlls/winewayland.drv/vulkan.c
@@ -97,2 +97,4 @@ static void wayland_map_device_extensions(struct vulkan_device_extensions *exten
     if (extensions->has_VK_KHR_external_fence_fd) extensions->has_VK_KHR_external_fence_win32 = 1;
+    extensions->has_VK_WINE_openvr_device_extensions = 1;
+    extensions->has_VK_WINE_openxr_device_extensions = 1;
 }
